For the final report of this directed study, I wrote a report documenting the probabilistic interpretation of the expander graphs (family). 
That is, random walks on them behave very similarly to independent sampling. 
One application of this property is to construct efficient sampler for simulation purposes (since pesudo-randomness is expansive). 
I give a small example of error reduction for random algorithms to demonstrate how such sampler can be useful. 

